---
import DetailLayout from "../layouts/DetailLayout.astro";
---
<DetailLayout title="Yangshuo Cycling Routes" subtitle="Three bike routes through karst peaks, rice paddies, and riverside villages — from easy 10km to challenging 40km."
  description="Detailed Yangshuo cycling routes: three self-guided bike routes with distances, terrain difficulty, rest stops, toilet locations, and downloadable maps.">

  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-6 mb-10">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-stone-400">Quick Picker</p>
    <div class="mt-3 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4">
        <p class="font-semibold text-stone-900">Route 1: Classic</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-stone-500">10 km · 1.5-2 hrs · Flat</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-accent">Best for first-time riders</p>
        <a href="#route1" class="mt-2 inline-block text-xs font-medium text-accent hover:underline">Jump to route</a>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4">
        <p class="font-semibold text-stone-900">Route 2: Riverside</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-stone-500">25 km · 3-4 hrs · Mostly flat</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-accent">Best scenery-to-effort ratio</p>
        <a href="#route2" class="mt-2 inline-block text-xs font-medium text-accent hover:underline">Jump to route</a>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4">
        <p class="font-semibold text-stone-900">Route 3: Explorer</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-stone-500">40 km · 5-6 hrs · Rolling hills</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-amber-600">For fit riders only</p>
        <a href="#route3" class="mt-2 inline-block text-xs font-medium text-accent hover:underline">Jump to route</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Before You Ride</h2>
  <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 mt-6">
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-3">Bike Rental</p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-600">
        <li>Standard bike: 30 RMB/day from any shop on West Street or Pan Tao Road</li>
        <li>E-bike: 50-80 RMB/day — highly recommended in summer heat</li>
        <li>No deposit required — just leave your hotel name</li>
        <li>Test the brakes before you leave</li>
        <li><strong>Recommended:</strong> Yangshuo Bike Rental (Pan Tao Rd, near the bus station). Well-maintained fleet, English-speaking owner.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-3">What to Bring</p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-600">
        <li>Water — at least 2L for routes 2 and 3. One bottle isn't enough.</li>
        <li>Sunscreen. No shade on most roads.</li>
        <li>Phone with offline map</li>
        <li>Cash — small shops and roadside vendors don't take Alipay from foreign accounts</li>
        <li>Rain jacket (May-September). Storms come fast.</li>
        <li>Toilet paper. Public toilets exist but rarely have it.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="route1" class="mt-12">Route 1: Ten Mile Gallery (Classic)</h2>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 my-4">
    <span class="rounded-full bg-accent/10 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-accent">10 km</span>
    <span class="rounded-full bg-stone-100 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-stone-500">1.5-2 hours</span>
    <span class="rounded-full bg-stone-100 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-stone-500">Flat</span>
    <span class="rounded-full bg-stone-100 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-stone-500">Paved</span>
  </div>
  <p>The classic. A flat 10 km road running alongside the Yulong River with karst peaks lining both sides. This is the ride everyone does — and for good reason. Best done early morning (7-8 AM start) to beat the tour buses and catch golden light on the peaks.</p>

  <div class="my-6 rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-3">Turn-by-Turn</p>
    <ol class="space-y-3 text-sm text-stone-600">
      <li><strong>Start:</strong> West Street. Head west on Diecui Road, cross the bridge.</li>
      <li><strong>1 km:</strong> Turn left onto Ten Mile Gallery road (Shili Hualang). Karst views start immediately.</li>
      <li><strong>3 km:</strong> Yulong River bridge — photo stop. Classic view: river winding through peaks.</li>
      <li><strong>5 km:</strong> Moon Hill trailhead on your left. Park bike, hike up (30-40 min).</li>
      <li><strong>7 km:</strong> Continue west. The road gets quieter. Pass villages with water buffalo in the fields.</li>
      <li><strong>10 km:</strong> Turnaround point. Small village with a noodle shop. Return same way or loop back through countryside roads.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="my-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 text-sm">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-4">
      <p class="font-semibold text-stone-700">Rest Stops</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-500">Yulong bridge drink vendors. Moon Hill entrance snack shop. Turnaround village noodle shop.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-4">
      <p class="font-semibold text-stone-700">Toilets</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-500">Moon Hill entrance (2 RMB). Yulong bridge public toilet. Noodle shop at turnaround.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-4">
      <p class="font-semibold text-stone-700">When to Go</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-500">Start by 7:30 AM. By 10 AM the road fills with tour buses. Late afternoon (4 PM) is also good.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="route2" class="mt-12">Route 2: Yulong River Loop (Riverside)</h2>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 my-4">
    <span class="rounded-full bg-accent/10 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-accent">25 km</span>
    <span class="rounded-full bg-stone-100 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-stone-500">3-4 hours</span>
    <span class="rounded-full bg-stone-100 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-stone-500">Mostly flat</span>
    <span class="rounded-full bg-stone-100 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-stone-500">Paved + dirt</span>
  </div>
  <p>The best scenery-to-effort ratio in Yangshuo. Follows the Yulong River through farmland, past ancient stone bridges, and through villages where you'll see exactly zero other tourists. Bring your camera — this is where the Instagram shots happen.</p>

  <div class="my-6 rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-3">Turn-by-Turn</p>
    <ol class="space-y-3 text-sm text-stone-600">
      <li><strong>Start:</strong> West Street. Head south toward the Yulong River.</li>
      <li><strong>3 km:</strong> Cross Dragon Bridge (Long Qiao). Take the dirt path on the right.</li>
      <li><strong>6 km:</strong> Fuli Bridge — a 400-year-old stone arch. Perfect photo spot with bamboo rafts passing below.</li>
      <li><strong>10 km:</strong> Path joins paved village road. Follow signs for Jiuxian Ancient Village.</li>
      <li><strong>14 km:</strong> Jiuxian Village. Stop here. Explore 200-year-old courtyard houses. Buy drinks at the well shop.</li>
      <li><strong>18 km:</strong> Yulong River bamboo raft launch point. Even without rafting, the river bend is stunning.</li>
      <li><strong>22 km:</strong> Cross back to the east side. Follow village roads back.</li>
      <li><strong>25 km:</strong> Return through northern countryside — rice paddies, duck farms, hilltop temple.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="my-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 text-sm">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-4">
      <p class="font-semibold text-stone-700">Rest Stops</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-500">Fuli Bridge drink vendor. Jiuxian Village shop. Yulong raft launch point restaurant.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-4">
      <p class="font-semibold text-stone-700">Toilets</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-500">Jiuxian Village public toilet. Yulong raft launch point toilets (2 RMB).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-4">
      <p class="font-semibold text-stone-700">Tip</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-500">Dirt path section (km 3-10) gets muddy after rain. E-bike handles it fine; standard bike will struggle.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="route3" class="mt-12">Route 3: Xingping Explorer (For Fit Riders)</h2>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 my-4">
    <span class="rounded-full bg-amber-100 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-amber-700">40 km</span>
    <span class="rounded-full bg-stone-100 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-stone-500">5-6 hours</span>
    <span class="rounded-full bg-stone-100 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-stone-500">Rolling hills</span>
    <span class="rounded-full bg-stone-100 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-stone-500">Paved + gravel</span>
  </div>
  <p>For cyclists who want to earn their views. Yangshuo to Xingping — the village on the 20 RMB banknote — through the most dramatic karst landscape. The reward: arriving at Laozhai Mountain at golden hour with no crowds.</p>

  <div class="my-6 rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-3">Turn-by-Turn</p>
    <ol class="space-y-3 text-sm text-stone-600">
      <li><strong>Start:</strong> Yangshuo town. Head south on S305 toward Xingping. Well-paved, moderate traffic.</li>
      <li><strong>8 km:</strong> First major hill. ~1 km steady climb. Views open up at the top.</li>
      <li><strong>15 km:</strong> Small village with truck-stop restaurant. Only reliable food stop before Xingping. Noodles or fried rice (15-20 RMB).</li>
      <li><strong>25 km:</strong> Descend into the valley. More dramatic peaks, Li River appears on your right.</li>
      <li><strong>32 km:</strong> Xingping town. Lock bike, walk to 20 RMB viewpoint (15 min).</li>
      <li><strong>Optional:</strong> Hike Laozhai Mountain (1,159 steps, 40 min up). Best river bend view in China. Tip 10 RMB at base shop to watch your bike.</li>
      <li><strong>Return:</strong> Take local bus back with bike (20 RMB extra). Or ride back — hills are worse in reverse.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="my-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 text-sm">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-4">
      <p class="font-semibold text-stone-700">Rest Stops</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-500">Truck-stop restaurant at km 15. Xingping town riverside restaurants (beer fish).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-4">
      <p class="font-semibold text-stone-700">Toilets</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-500">Restaurant at km 15. Xingping public toilets near bus station and 20 RMB viewpoint.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-4">
      <p class="font-semibold text-amber-800">Important</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-amber-700">Start by 6:30 AM in summer. Bring 3L+ water per person. E-bike highly recommended — hills will destroy you on a standard bike.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-6">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-stone-400">Route Comparison</p>
    <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
        <thead class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-stone-400">
          <tr><th class="pb-2 pr-4">Route</th><th class="pb-2 pr-4">Distance</th><th class="pb-2 pr-4">Time</th><th class="pb-2 pr-4">Difficulty</th><th class="pb-2">Best For</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-stone-100">
          <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium text-stone-900">Classic</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">10 km</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">1.5-2 hrs</td><td class="py-2 pr-4"><span class="text-accent">Easy</span></td><td class="py-2">First-time riders, families, photo stops</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium text-stone-900">Riverside</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">25 km</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">3-4 hrs</td><td class="py-2 pr-4"><span class="text-accent">Moderate</span></td><td class="py-2">Scenery lovers, photographers, half-day trip</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium text-stone-900">Explorer</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">40 km</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">5-6 hrs</td><td class="py-2 pr-4"><span class="text-amber-600">Hard</span></td><td class="py-2">Fit cyclists, full-day adventure, golden hour</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-6">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-stone-400">Continue Reading</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm">
      <li><a href="/ten-mile-gallery" class="text-accent hover:underline">Ten Mile Gallery</a></li>
      <li><a href="/moon-hill" class="text-accent hover:underline">Moon Hill</a></li>
      <li><a href="/yulong-river-bamboo-raft" class="text-accent hover:underline">Yulong River Bamboo Raft</a></li>
      <li><a href="/yangshuo-travel-guide" class="text-accent hover:underline">Yangshuo Travel Guide</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

</DetailLayout>
